# Cloudflare static-asset headers. (Not applied by `npm run dev` — checked 2026-11-24 — so the CSP
# can't break hot reload; `npm run test:csp` checks it against a production build.)

# Every page and asset: security headers. The CSP allows only our own files; the one inline
# script (the pre-paint theme script in index.html) is allowed by its sha256 — if that script
# changes, test/client/theme.test.ts names the new hash to put here. Inline style ATTRIBUTES are
# not allowed; setting element.style from code (drag transforms, CSS variables) is unaffected.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-9LkzLocWtXQtb5eFdCIxhOVvwqJUaIp6dKQgngULrwk='; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# Vite's hashed bundles never change content under the same name → cache forever.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# HTML (the app shell, also served for join links via the SPA fallback) must always be
# revalidated, so a reload after a deploy gets the new bundle (OUTDATED_CLIENT, CLAUDE.md §6).
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/g/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
